---
import ShellLayout from "../layouts/ShellLayout.astro";
import ScaffoldBanner from "../components/ScaffoldBanner.astro";
---
<ShellLayout title="Method — Neoplastix" current="method">
  <ScaffoldBanner seat={4} handle="Yassin-Skirej" title="Wave A scaffold" />
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Method</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      How a painting becomes a schema-valid study, a catalog artefact, and a
      public page — with uncertainty named.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Measure</h2>
    <p>
      An instructor or student records catalogue identity, reproduction pixel
      size and crop, then places normalized points, coloured rectangles and
      explicit black lines. Wall time and σ live in <code>MEASUREMENT.md</code>.
      Review status stays <code>proposal</code> until a second pass accepts it.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Schema</h2>
    <p>
      <code>work.schema.json</code> is the contract. Ajv, zod, JS semantic checks
      and pydantic must agree on fixtures. Derived tracks are never written back
      into <code>work.yml</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Classical geometry (prior art)</h2>
    <p>
      The point / rectangle / explicit-line representation adapts Andrzejewski
      et al. (2010), §3.2 — not the paper’s classifier or generator
      (Andrzejewski, 2010). Public pages never embed vault node IDs.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Catalog build</h2>
    <p>
      Python emits <code>public/patterns/&lt;id&gt;.json|.svg</code> and MVP
      geometric variations at build time. Preset buttons load those files; they
      do not call FastAPI.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Dual render</h2>
    <p>
      One render plan serialises to CSS Grid (gallery / About pedagogy) and SVG
      (editor / export). Planes sit below lines; thickness comes from derived
      geometry only.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Uncertainty and rights</h2>
    <p>
      Every published study carries EU and US rights rows and a credit that the
      artefact is a geometric study after the named work — not a museum
      photograph (D-32). Incomplete rights keep a work out of the public build.
    </p>
  </article>
</ShellLayout>
